🔐 Realtime Checkbox Sync with OAuth 2.0 + OpenID Connect


Demo:-
youtube:-https://youtu.be/eSu6Hg00hAE

A full-stack real-time application that combines WebSockets (Socket.IO) with a custom-built OAuth 2.0 + OpenID Connect authentication system.

Users can view a shared checkbox grid in real time, but only authenticated users are allowed to modify it.

🚀 Features
🔐 OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code Flow (Custom Built)
🧠 OpenID Connect (OIDC) for user identity
🍪 JWT-based authentication stored in HTTP-only cookies
⚡ Realtime updates using Socket.IO + Redis Pub/Sub
👀 Public read access (anyone can view)
✏️ Restricted write access (only logged-in users can update)
⏱️ Session expiration using JWT + cookie maxAge
🚫 Unauthorized socket connections are blocked
🏗️ Architecture
1. Authorization Server (Port 8000)

Handles:

Login
Consent
Authorization Code generation
Token exchange (/token)
JWT issuance
2. Realtime App Server (Port 9000)

Handles:

OAuth client flow (/login, /callback)
Cookie storage
Socket authentication
Checkbox sync logic
Redis Pub/Sub
3. Redis

Used for:

Broadcasting checkbox updates across instances
4. MongoDB

Stores:

Checkbox state
🔁 Full Flow
1. User clicks Login
GET /login

Redirects to:

http://localhost:8000/authorize
2. Authorization Flow
User logs in
Gives consent
Gets redirected back:
http://localhost:9000/callback?code=abc123
3. Token Exchange
POST http://localhost:8000/token

Response:

{
  "access_token": "jwt_token"
}
4. Cookie Storage
res.cookie("access_token", token, {
  httpOnly: true,
  maxAge: 30 * 1000
});
5. Socket Authentication
io.use((socket, next) => {
  const token = socket.request.cookies?.access_token;

  if (!token) return next(new Error("Unauthorized"));

  try {
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
    socket.user = decoded;
    next();
  } catch {
    next(new Error("Unauthorized"));
  }
});

6. Realtime Updates

Client emits:

socket.emit("client:checkbox:change", { index, checked });
Server publishes via Redis
All clients receive:
io.emit("server:checkbox:change", data);

🔒 Access Control

User Type	View	Modify

Guest	✅	❌
Logged-in	✅	✅
⏱️ Session Handling
JWT contains expiry (exp)
Cookie uses maxAge
On expiry:
Socket reconnect fails
User becomes unauthorized


📁 Project Structure
.
