⚙️ Environment Variables
Realtime App (.env)
PORT=9000
CLIENT_ID=your_client_id
CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret
REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:9000/callback
JWT_SECRET=1234567890
Auth Server (.env)
PORT=8000
JWT_SECRET=1234567890

👉 ⚠️ JWT_SECRET must match in both servers

🧪 How to Run


1. Start MongoDB

mongod

2. Start Redis
redis-server

3. Start Auth Server
cd openid-server

npm install

npm start

4. Start Realtime App
cd realtime-app
npm install
npm start

5. Open in browser
http://localhost:9000


🎯 Key Learnings


OAuth 2.0 is authorization, not authentication
OpenID Connect adds identity layer
JWT enables stateless auth
WebSockets require separate auth handling
Cookies + JWT must be aligned for expiry
Redis enables horizontal scalability
⚠️ Limitations (Intentional)
No refresh tokens
No PKCE
No HTTPS (secure cookies disabled)
No token revocation
Basic error handling
🚀 Future Improvements
Add refresh tokens
Implement PKCE
Use secure cookies (HTTPS)
Add logout endpoint
Role-based access control
Socket reconnection with token refresh